hi everyone!



for those interested in linux audio development, the linux audio=20
conference 2005 (http://lac.zkm.de) at the center for arts and media in=20
karlsruhe/germany will be streamed live in both vorbis and theora formats=
.

the conference takes place from april 21 - 24, with lectures and=20
workshops from 11:00 to 18:00 UTC+2 every day and concerts in the evening=
s.

i would like to invite you to join us, either in person (attendance to=20
the conference is free) or remotely over the internet.

for remote participants of the conference, there is a chat room #lac2005=20
on irc.freenode.net. a chat operator will be present in the auditorium=20
in karlsruhe and will relay your questions to the lecturer and the local=20
audience. papers and slides will be made available for download in=20
advance if possible.

information about the streams and how to watch them is at=20
http://lac2005.zkm.de.

huge kudos to the icecast, ogg, vorbis and theora developers and=20
communites for their code and expertise!



kind regards,


j=F6rn nettingsmeier
on behalf of the linux audio community



